$DIR/main.p:41:2: the init function of package main at main.p:38 can start a task during package initialization
    Package initialization must finish before another task can read package
    variables.
    The init function of package main at main.p:38 calls scope.Task (main.p:41),
    which starts a task.
    Tasks may read package variables written only during initialization without
    a lock. Finishing initialization before starting another task preserves that
    data race rule.
    Start the task from main or a function main calls
    (see "Package initialization" in the Plutonium spec, section 15.2)
    (run "pluto explain E2587" for a longer explanation)

